From d069f0dfbbaf1602822717d2c0455cc4c279a30b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Witold=20Gre=C5=84?= <witold.gren@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 16:54:21 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] push: parse ';'-separated FCM crypto headers, keep token on
 unreadable message

Reolink sends crypto-key as "dh=...;p256ecdsa=...". fcm-push-listener 4.1.1
base64-decoded everything after "dh=", so every push failed with
"Invalid symbol 59" and Neolink cleared the token, re-registered and got
PHONE_REGISTRATION_ERROR. Vendor the crate with a header parameter parser
and only clear the token on crypto/dependency errors.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
